From 3151701c141ab900f15e3c657a0b4366c31c8c87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Proofloom Contributor <proofloom-contributor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:46:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show example and corrected sentence for each replacement in
 the assistant pane

Every card in the writing assistant now quotes the sentence that contains
the flagged text and rewrites it with the chosen replacement, so the
suggestion can be judged in context instead of as an isolated word pair.

- Add src/core/sentence.js: a DOM-free sentenceContext() helper that finds
  the sentence containing an issue range (bounded scan, breaks on sentence
  punctuation including CJK/Arabic terminators and line breaks, keeps
  decimals intact) and returns the example sentence, the corrected
  sentence, the offsets to mark, and window-clip flags.
- Render the two rows in each assistant card; the corrected row follows
  the alternative picked in the card's dropdown, and cards without a
  replacement show the example sentence on its own.
- Pass the current chapter text into assistantView from renderAssistant.
- Style the rows to match the card design; flagged text keeps the red
  del treatment, the replacement gets the green ins pill, clipped
  sentences get ellipsis markers.
- Cover the helper with tests/sentence.test.mjs (13 cases).
